# Everything the image does not need, kept out of the build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the one that bites: a smaller context is a
# faster build, but a context that changes is a *cache miss*, and `.git`,
# `__pycache__` and a profiling dump change constantly.  Leaving them in meant
# every build re-installed every dependency.
.git
.github
.claude
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
dist
build
*.egg-info
docs
docs/_build
tests
conftest.py
noxfile.py
tasks.py
program.prof
*.prof
uv.lock
CHANGELOG.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
# Debug dumps the scraper writes beside itself when a page will not parse.
debug_*.html
_diag*.py
